That particular one has been there since Berzerkely, it got me when I went
from a V7 Unix (where su left you in the current directory) to BSD (around
1986 ? - in which an su took you to the home directory of the user su'd to ;-)

>I got to figure out how to restore osfboot and vmunix from the CDROM
>as a result of...

>    $ pwd
>    /usr/somewhere
>    $ rm *
>    foo: permission denied
>    $ su
