Steve Rosen (smrosen@ceres.rm.fccc.edu) wrote:
: I found glitch in 'su' running under 4.3 where it accepts the typed
: password and then just hangs.  There appears to be a permission
: problem of some sort, but I can't find anything specific.  After
: talking with DEC C/S, their fix was to reboot the machine and it goes
: away.  This is true, but the problem always returns in time.  Anybody
: know what the permanent fix is for this? 


     I posted about this in comp.unix.admin recently, and got several
responses.  I t appears that su is trying to write to /dev/console
when /dev/console is hung.  Therefore, su hangs.  The following perl
script (sent to me by Greg Thain) supposedly "unhangs" /dev/console,
which ought to clear up the problem.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
#!/usr/local/bin/perl
# Send the TIOCSTART ioctl to the console

require "sys/ioctl.ph";
open(CO,"/dev/console") || die("can't open /dev/console:$!");
ioctl(CO,&TIOCSTART,$foo) || die("ioctl failed: $!");

---------------------------------------------------------------------

     Someone else suggested that it may be related to the syslog -
perhaps your syslog is dead or hung when this happens?  I believe su
talks to the syslog as well.

