Yes, some systems are in easily accessed areas. Why? because of different
reasons beyond my control. Some of the satellites are also allowed to do 
conversational boots,so that they can boot with a different set of parameters
for different  applications (we used to have one set for VWS and one for DECW)
You have to remember that not every site has all its systems behind the 
security of a locked computer room.
The point remains that in a non-secured environment, it is hard to maintain
security and, therefore, one should not make the situation worse.
I know that the information is available in the VMS manual set, and for 
someone who wants to find it, it will be trivial. This is not my worry.
I am more concerned with someone who sees this information posted, and decides
to give it a try.
I do not agree with the argument that since the information exists in the
manual, then it is ok to post it. You can also go to your local library and
find information on how to make all sorts of illegal substances. Do you then
think it is ok to post it ?

I believe that security related questions should be answered by e-mail.
We should take a look at how security announcements are posted by CERT, and
do the same.

