glenn@sundeck.usask.ca (Glenn Hollinger) writes:
}Here are two questions for all the DECstation experts out there.
}1. How many PMAZ turbochannel SCSI option cards are supported under
}Ultrix 4.3 in a DECstation 5000/125 box?  Three cards will fit, but
}will the OS talk to all three as well as the on-board SCSI channel?

We have used all 4 (I was curious too...) in a 5000/240 so it seems
quite likely that 4 can be used in /125 too.  We routinely use
3 SCSI + 1 FDDI.

}2. There are two numbers given as the peak I/O throughput of the
}turbochannel, 40MB/sec for DMA transfers (512 bytes at a time)
}and 5MB/sec for 'protocol limited' transfers.  Which number
}applies to disk reads/writes under Ultrix 4.3?

Each SCSI channel has a "limit" of 5 MB/s.  Under Ultrix 4.3
I have got 2.5MB/s peak out of a single disk (a RZ25).  The
newer disks are probably this fast or faster.

Depending on your I/O workload, you may very well find yourself
"seek limited" rather than bandwidth limited.  The reciprocal of
the average seek time is a good indication of the maximum seeks/second
you can get out the disk (perhaps twice that if your seeks have good
locality of reference).  [In my experience, your mileage may vary]

