The Ultrix 4.3 scsi driver seems to have some problems going over 3.5 Mb/s,
(5000/240, 2.5 Mb/s on a 5000/33). If you have 2 disks, raw read from
both at the same time seems to add up to about 3.5 Mb, anyway far below
5 Mb/s. But if you have 2 scsi controllers reading from the other doesn't
affect the other. So if you have a disk that can give you sustained > 
3.5 Mb/s, then you should have one controller/disk. In practice this
is necessary only if you use diskstriping, and huge sequential reads/writes..
