In article <1993Apr28.140912.4403@alw.nih.gov>, howardy@freud.nia.nih.gov (Howard Wai-Chun Yeung) writes:
>
> [ I believe this is the original author who has discovered that
>   ULTRIX doesn't support mmap and family. ]
>
>That's not a good news to me.
>Actually, the program isn't written by me.  I guess the original
>author is trying to map a protion of memeory to an output file.
>
>Is there an equivalent function in Ultrix c which do the same
>thing, or any ways to get around this?

It depends exactly what "this" is.  If the intent is to have a
chunk of what's in memory end up in a file, then the good old
fashioned way is likely to work:

	if((fd = open("file", O_WRONLY)) == -1 )
		/* handle error */
	else {
		rc = write(fd, buffer, size) ;

		if( rc != WHAT_IS_EXPECTED )
			/* handle that error */

		if( close(fd) == -1 )
			/* Handle that error */
	}

If there is more going on than simply moving bytes of memory to a file,
then a more complex solution may be necessary.

