Steven,
 
I have been using exactly the technique you describe for many 
years (since DECnet-VAX first supported Async lines).
 
From your description, it sounds like one or both sides of the 
connection are not configured properly. 
 
In particular, you want to make sure that the connection uses 
dynamic async DECnet, in which the line reverts to normal 
terminal use after a disconnection.  Terminating a connection 
requires some privileges, but it is not too difficult (you shut 
down the circuit/line and clear it). My apologies, I don't 
happen to have a sample of the commands handy at the moment.
 
If I can be of further assistance, please feel free to contact me 
via Email or phone.
 
