I presume you did a kill -1 1 ? Otherwisse init doesn't recognize your
new change to /ewtc/ttys and will not start a getty. If DTR isn't high
no modem will answer.

>Using a breakout box I see some strange things happening. Line 20 (DTR)
>seems to flip back and forth between high and low. If I set line 20 high
>then the modem answers but getty doesn't fire up a login. I'm confused!

Are you using DECs cable and connector - it has certain RS232 pins
wired together. If you are not, then it is possible that DSR (pin 6)
is not high or some other pin is not high. Make sure RTS/CTS/DSR
(4-5-6) are all high.
