^B followed by a string of digits (some characters like '(' and '-'
are ignored) and a <return> dials the number (if your unit is a DF03-AC)

^A is supposed to work also, but I don't remember the specific use.

^G will take the modem off-hook, in case you dial the remote machine
using the telephone pad.

^C aborts ^A and ^B commands.

