In an article not present in my news spool, someone writes:

> I've got an OEM system containing an 11/73 processor.  Every couple of
> days, the system stops.  No errors, no red lights on the CPU or memory
> cards, no nothing.  I realize that I'm grasping for a straw here, but
> does anyone have any clues as too what to try to isolate the problem?

  Is this system in a BA23 or BA123 enclosure? DEC had a problem with the
wiring harnesses in those systems which caused erratic operation (and could
lead to fires in the cabinet eventually). The way to tell is to look at the
harness (1 in the BA23, 2 in the BA123) between the power supply and the
backplane. There are 3 possible styles: individual wires with yellow con-
nectors, webbed wires, and individual wires with white connectors. Only the
last style is safe. Note that if this is your problem there is probably
melted plastic coating some of the power supply/backplane connector pins,
and you will have to carefully clean them.

