mlevin@husc8.harvard.edu (Michael Levin) writes...
> 
>     Suppose I have a program, written in C on a VMS system. How do I
>tell within the prorgram if it happens to be running alone, or inside
>the VMS debugger? I want a function in_debug() which I can use as
>follows. Is there some system call or something?
> 

There is a P1-space longword CTL$GL_PSTFLAGS.  If the USRI$V_DBG_MAPPED
bit in this longword is set, the debugger is mapped.  How you code this
in C I'll leave up to you.  You have to link against SYS$SYSTEM:SYS.STB
to access this value.  Also, this is undocumented and unsupported, but
the Fortran RTL uses this so I doubt it will change.  The USRI$ symbols
are defined in USRIDEF.H.

I don't know if this works on AXP systems.

