After asking DEC, I found this juicy tidbit for all you VAXstation 4000 owners:
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The VAX MOTIF V1.1 "decsound" application, although it is normally
windows-based, *CAN* be used at the command level, with NO windows,
to play sound files.   There are unix-like command-line options
available, and no, these are *NOT* documented.

(prime example:   enable SOUNDS to be played on the vaxstation when
triggered by Vaxcluster Console System [VCS] events, which is all
done via detached processes........).

$ decsound :== $sys$system:decsound.exe
$ decsound -play somefile.aud [-volume nnn] [-speaker | -headphone]

"nnn" for the volume is in the range of 1-100.  The default is whatever
your OWN personal saved defaults are.   I also believe the default for
the latter parameter is "-headphone"....


A side note:   Since the dec soundchip uses u-law, SUN ".au" files
*WILL* work quite well.

(someone pass this along to guido to include in his sound formats guide)


