The process is quite simple. 
 
   - Perform a conversational boot (B/R5:1 xx, where xx is the 
     name of the disk drive which the system is on, usually DU0)
 
   - When you get the prompt from SYSBOOT, enter the following 
     commands:
 
               SET /STARTUP=OPA:
               CONTINUE
 
   - When the system boots, you will get the dollar sign prompt.
 
   - Enter the following commands (note: These commands are 
     different under VMS 4.x than under 5.x):
 
               SPAWN
               @[SYS0.SYSEXE]STARTUP
 
    - When the startup file completes, you will once again 
      receive the "$" prompt. At this point, you are logged into
      SYSTEM, with full privileges. All of the logical names are
      also defined. You can now use AUTHORIZE.
 
I believe that the above description is complete. If I have been 
unclear, or if I can be of further assistance, please feel free 
to contact me via Email or phone.
 
