> 1) Can anyone tell me what the real difference is between these two boxes?
> The DECdirect catalog says that the 3000/400 is 108.1 SPECmarks and the
> 3000/500 is 121.5 SPECmarks.  Yet, from the descriptions, the two machines
> (at least in their basic configurations) are identical.  Is it just a
> difference in the clock speed, or is there some other substantive hardware
> difference?

The motherboard is essentially the same. On the /400 the motherboard video
is not stuffed and the connectors go out the other way (the I/O board mounts
on the other side in the /500). I would expect that PALs etc. on the /400
are slower, so you probably won't be able to up the clock rate.

