We have some DEC VXT-2000 X-termials which we want to run VUE sessions from an
HP 9000/750.  The VXT-2000 has a built-in version of mwm which runs locally.
It can be configured to exit when another window manager tries to start on that
display.  When I start an IP-based X session from the Terminal Manager window
on the VXT, I get the vuelogin screen (with Motif window dressing), and I can
login.  Right after the vuelogin screen goes away, I get a brief glimpse of the
vuehello screen (normally shows the /etc/copyright file), then it goes back to
the Terminal Manager window with the local mwm.  The message in the
$HOME/.vue/errorlog file is:

  <unknown program name>: Another vuesession is currently running - exiting.

If I configure the local window manager to not allow remote window managers to
run, then the rest of the session (except for vuewm) seems to start fine.

This happens most of the time, though there have been a couple times when it 
did seem to start everything correctly.

What I am wondering is, does anyone have any ideas about why this is happening?
Is this a problem on the HP side, or on the DEC VXT side?  What can I do to
correct it?

Also, does anyone know of a way to disable the local window manager
entirely?  I can't seem to find anything in the documentation or the menus which
would suggest it is a possibility.

