I am associated with a company which has developed an interface
which sits at the end of the Dec Massbus and emulates from 1 to 8
RP07/RP06 type devices.  This device has been designed to cope with 
the 18 bit massbus from the RH-20 of a KL-10.  This unit will likely
be offered as a commercial product in the near future if there is any
demand for it at all (ie greater than 10 units).

The interface consists of a CPU and some memory which allows SCSI
disks (commercial, off the shelf) to be attached to it, and makes them
look like RP07/RP06 drives.  In both our testing and the customers
we have found that the drives perform about 10-15% better than the
real RP07/RP06 drives.

This device needs no changes to be made to any applications or the
Monitor running on the KL-10.  We have tested this unit with both
TOPS-10 and TOPS-20.  If your site runs a different operating system
the device will likely work but customization is available.

A version of this unit will be available for 16 bit massbus within
the next few months.

If you are interested in more technical details, you may call me
Richard Snider, or Jaan Luts at +1 416 968 7155 between 9-5 EST.

