   There is a utility called 10BACKUP which I have on my system.
   Not sure if we have the "latest".  It has also not been used
   in a *long* time.  TOPS-10 had a BACKUP utility.  TOPS-20 called
   their version DUMPER.  There was an "interchange" mode for reading
   one another's files (I think the main difference was the directory
   structure).  I know 10BACKUP worked (past tense) on TOPS-10 tapes
   (VMS 4.x).  I *believe* it was intended to work for TOPS-20 tapes
   as well, but I don't *know* that it did.

   Here is the 1st screen of the help file for 10BACKUP:


$ help 10backup
10BACKUP
                         10BACKUP v2.1

        10BACKUP is a VAX  program  to  read  DECsystem-10  BACKUP  format
   tapes.

        10BACKUP has two primary functions; to get directories of, and  to
   selectively   restore   files   from  tapes  written  by  BACKUP  on  a
   DECsystem-10.

        Because of differences between the DEC-10 and the VAX this program
   is  intended  mainly for restoring ASCII files.  Limited facilities for
   restoring binary information are available through the SIXBIT command.


  Additional information available:

  USE        EXIT       TAPE       SSNAME     DIR        RESTORE    FILE
  REWIND     SKIP       SIXBIT     INTER      DETAIL

$

   10BACKUP sources are available here via anonymous FTP (to hydra.uwo.ca).
   CD to "tape_utilities" and then to "10backup".  There is a "sources"
   directory one notch further down as well.  Looks like most of 10BACKUP
   was written in BASIC.

   If necessary, I can package everything using VMS_SHARE and email it.
   Let me know.  Chow,  b.
