Not quite. The DEC-10 program was called BACKUP and the DEC-20 (tops20)
variant was called DUMPER. They could read/write tapes for each other
in 'INTERCHANGE' mode. At least one of the PD VAX readers assumed
the tape was written in this format and you were stuck if it wasn't.

Two different readers were supplied by DEC on the TOPS/VMS tools
tape (free to anyone who asked) and they may still ship the tape
if you can find someone inside DEC who remembers life before VAX.
