	There were two DEC operating systems for 36-bit machines
Tops-10 and Tops20. The Tops-10 backup utility was called BACKUP
and the Tops-20 utility was called DUMPER.

	In the days of V4 VMS, DEC supplied a tools conversion tape
that included DUMPER and 10BACKUP utilities designed to help sites
convert from the TOPS operating systems to VMS. If the tape has the
word `interchange' on it, it was writen in a mode that could be read
by either BACKUP or DUMPER.

	I haven't seen the tools conversion tape for quite some time,
but maybe someone out there as the tape or the tools in an archive.


