Update (Curtin Uni DEC-10):
The DEC-10 eventually died when some contaminant (?chlorine) got
into the computer airconditioning and randomly dissolved circuit board
tracks. (It took several years and much chemical analysis to find the
problem.)
The terminal room is now full of PCs and Macs on the network which is
linked to the various VAXen. (So it can still be used as a terminal room.)
The plate glass windows are still in place, but are now considered a fire
hazard. (We're supposed to replace the glass with bricks.)
The Muzak was disconnected many years ago, though all the old ceiling
speakers are still here. We now do our own thing with u-beaut multi-media 
systems.


