In article <1993Apr7.130333.452@cu23.crl.aecl.ca>, Glen Reesor writes:


>I just received a DECstation 3100 for use as an X-terminal (it's only got 8
>Megs of RAM, so isn't use for much more :-) and I would like to have the
>numeric keypad send application keypad codes for ALL of my X clients.

Do you really mean *all* X clients or just xterm and dxterm?

>I can configure the DECterm's to send the application keycodes by setting
>"Application Keypad" in the Customize/General menu.  However, if I log into
>another machine (in this case an SGI) and send back an xterm, I can't get
>the keypad to send anything but numbers.

To set xterm to send application keycodes, send it the DECKPAN (DEC KeyPad
Application Mode) sequence (<ESC>=).  To reset back to the defaul numeric
keypad mode, send the DECKPNM (DEC KeyPad Numeric Mode) sequence (<ESC>>).
If this escape sequence doesn't work for you, then try the DECNKM (DEC Numeric
Keypad Mode) sequences: <ESC>?66h to send application sequences, and <ESC>?66l
to reset back to numeric mode.  All these sequences should also work for dxterm
(DECterm).
 
