>We just got a VAXstation 2000 with a broken colour frame buffer and would
>like to connect a dumb (VT100-like) terminal to the serial port and boot
>it with that as the console. Is that possible, and if so - how do we do it?
>(Ie, what pins are used and things like that) I think it has Ultrix loaded
>on the hard disk. (A sticker on the back says "Model: VS410-C3", if that is
>of any help).

I can't speak about all VS2000's, but I have converted a number of them
so that I can attach a normal terminal as the console.  It depends on the
setting of a jumper (and some associated roms) on the motherboard
itself.  But the boot roms have to be a certain set...  Also, you'll
need an option which plugs into the video and printer ports and which
has three modified-RJ jacks to which you can attach terminals.

When I'm where my manuals are, I'll check and post the applicable
information.



