>   I'm receiving the following error on an 11-785 running Ultrix 3.1, and
>I've looked in quite a few books, and I'm not sure how to decipher it.
>This error occurs in spurts (5 or 10 at one time) and disappears for
>hours.

This error, well actually it's not an error, can occur in the following 
circumstances:

The processor notes that a lower priority interrupt has been requested, but
not granted. Normally when IPL falls below the device interrupts level, the
interrupt will be granted and serviced. If however the device/adapter is no 
longer requesting an interrupt at that time the system is unable to determine
which interrupt service routine to call. In this case a counter is increased,
an errorlog entry is written and the interrupt is dismissed without beeing 
served.


