	As I remember, there was also a dual personality disk. The disk had
	the first part formatted in 16-bit mode, readable by the PDP11. The
	PDP11 booted itself, then gave control of the disk to the KL10, and
	kickstarted the KL10, which read from the rest of the disk, which was
	36-bit data.

