    Well, you seem to have ignored all the warnings that you're running
Field Test versions of VMS and Fortran, etc., (an early FT version of
VMS at that), and that all sorts of internal checks have been turned on
which slow things down, a lot in some cases.

    In particular, there was a note about 6 weeks ago, I believe in 
comp.sys.dec, about the slowness of FORTRAN I/O on OpenVMS-AXP.  There
are data conversion routines in the Fortran run-time library (to do
big-endian/little-endian, or IEEE/VAX, etc.), and it turns out these
were converting native VMS _to_ native VMS, unconditionally, ALWAYS.  
So your I/O benchmarks are WAY OFF what the production VMS will give you.  
BTW, I believe this is corrected in VMS V1.5-FT, but I've no way to verify 
that...

