I used to work on a KL10 system that had a flakey interface between the
11 and the 10, the 11 would report that the 10 was down even when it
wasn't, and the system would have to be take down in order for the
two to estalish communication again.

This got to be so annoying that it was decided that if the -11 died, to
just ignore it and continue work.

Since the front-end was an 11/40, I used to boot up RT-11 from dectapes
and work on my own stand-alone programs (I was working on implementing
a simple O/S for a college project at the time).

The 'back-end' continued happily running TOPS-10 without a problem.

