It's too bad you have a less-than-perfect sales rep, but if you want
complete SPECmark information (and other benchmarks) for most of our
systems, use anonymous FTP to get the info from gatekeeper.dec.com.
The directory is DEC/DECinfo/performance-summary, and here is a list
of the .ps files (as of today):
    alpha-axp-openvms-server.ps             decsys-5000-240-tpc-a.ps
    alpha-axp-openvms-workstation.ps        decsys-5000-25-tpc-b.ps
    alpha-axp-openvms-xllperf.ps            decsys-5100-tpc-a.ps
    alpha-axp-osf1-aim-chart.ps             decsys-5100-tpc-b.ps
    alpha-axp-osf1-server.ps                decsys-5500-tpc-a.ps
    alpha-axp-osf1-svr-flash.ps             decsys-5500-tpc-b.ps
    alpha-axp-osf1-workstation.ps           decsys-family.ps
    alpha-axp-osf1-ws-flash.ps              vaxstation-family.ps
    decsta-family.ps

"decsta-family.ps" has the info you want, for DEC MIPS-based
workstations:
    Digital's DECstation Family Performance Summary      56 Pages of Postscript
    
    SPECmarks, Dhrystone, Whetstone, Linpack, DR Labs CPU2,
    Khornerstone, SoftPC, X11perf and PLB for the DECstation 5000
    product line (20, 25, 120, 125, 133, 200 and 240).
    
    Apr 1992
    
"decsys-family.ps" is what you want for MIPS-based servers.  Check out
the *.abs files or the "index" file.  And the *.ps files are available
compressed, as *.ps.Z

-Jeff


