	I have an 11/44 with UDA50/RA81, DEUNA, DZ, TU10, Emulex UC-18 (dual
SCSI) with Fuji 650 MB drive, RL11, TU77, and a few non-DEC, non-DMA interfaces
(and NO empty slots :-). This puppy definitely keeps the room warm. Anyway,
under RSX11M+, when I run the I/O exerciser, IOX, configuring one RL02, the
SCSI drive (looks like DU:), and the RA81, I invariably get a lot of (soft)
data late errors on the RL02 device.  According to the error logger, these
errors always recover on the first retry.  When ran by itself, the RL02 gives
no such errors, so I have a bus (timing) load (overload) problem, no? (All the
controllers in question are on BR5, BTW.)

	My question to the assembled wisdom: Would there be any point to my
(a) rearranging the bus to put the RL11 closer to the CPU (I don't remember
where I have it right now), or (b) increasing the 'backoff' parameter in the
UC-18 firmware so it's less of a bus hog, or (c) reconfiguring the UDA (a
jumper??) to become less of a bus hog, or (d) something else I haven't
thought of? Or maybe, the bus is truly overloaded and I've hit the hard
ceiling on Unibus throughput?

	In the way of evidence, I note that the RA81 has about 30% more
blocks transferred than the SCSI disk, per IOX run. No idea whether that's
significant or not.

	Ideas, suggestions, hints, flames, etc. are welcomed. Thanx.
