rack (viewed from the front), the DEC-10 parts are wider.

It's pretty easy to key in a light flashing program.  You can use the "RESET"
instruction as a nice time delay (I believe it also forces r0 into the lights.).
I used to key in a game that xors the switches with the lights and then rotates
the register.  The object is to extinguish the lights.

The fact that the 11/40 probably also has core memory means this will persist
for a long time.

