I always thought that the MSCP devices had to go at the _end_ of the bus.

You could also try the upping the Unibus delay on the UDA-50 to prevent
Unibus overloading. The install manual calls for at least 6.2 usec for a /44
with RL02 drives - with that mix of stuff you may want to go to 10 usec.

What DMA burst size and/or dwell time do you have your Emulex controller set
to? Try lowering/raising them too. 

BTW: 

We run one of our 11/84's with a UDA50/RA81, CMD CDU720 (scsi <=> mscp disk
and tape), Emulex TC13, Emulex SC21, 2 DHU11'S, DEUNA, and 3 LP11's.  
