>
>"Open" has nothing to do with end-user binary licensing policies.
That is not the point.
Just to cite from SPD 25.01.34, p.15 (VMS 5.4):
'Not all VMS license types are available for all system models.'

This means that DEC reserves the right to refuse selling licenses for
some systems even to customers who are willing to pay the license. And
there are indeed some processors (workstations and servers) which are
able to be used as interactive VMS systems, but only hindered by DEC's
braindead licensing policy. 

Further, it is well known that any limit on the count of interactive users that
is not far above the maximum of real users will tend to make the system
unusable for those who are supposed to use the system. Just one terminal
server port may cost you (at default 4) a lot of interactive user
