	PCs *SUCK* technically, but they are the *MOST* "open" system
out there!!

	One of my criteria for openness was always that the specs be
clearly published and that you be able to code to them without a lot
of threat of legal action. As far as interconnection and interoperation
go, PCs are amazing!!! I can run software from just about any vendor on
a PC, and it'll work. I can buy hardware from just about any vendor
and plug it in and it'll work. I can buy disk drives practically on
street corners that will work with my PC. Yes, you can do that with
some workstations, but the prices will make your ears bleed. I can
even buy 3rd party ROM for my PC, or I can burn my own, because there
are ROM codes published and for sale. I can buy just about any component
of a PC in isolation or as a complete system, from any of thousands
of vendors, and they will ALL interoperate. I can buy motherboard
layouts, chipsets, and compatible CPUs from 20 different vendors.
I can buy 50 or 60 different operating systems to run on the machine,
and I can get sources for some of them for free.

	Most importantly, I can design a board for the PC without
having to pay licensing fees to a vendor for doing so. I can design
a DOS or Windows device driver and sell it without having to pay
licensing fees. (Ever build a board that uses MSCP? Or make compatible
memory for a VAX?)

	At a software level, despite a lot of ugliness, there is
a high degree of interoperability in the PC world. There are only
de facto standards, which IMHO is good, since things that don't work
die out. On the other hand, my text editor (MS word) can read and
write files created by its 8 top competitiors. I run PC-NFS and
share my files with a Sun. If I don't like PC-NFS I can buy another
network stack in a matter of a few hours.

	PCs *SUCK* technically, but they are the *MOST* "open" system
out there!!

	If you say
>Open doesn't mean cheap, or widely available, or even sane and coherent. It
>means interconnectible and interoperable.
	then I can't possibly see what's not open about PCs!! It's
UNIX(tm) and OpenVMS(tm) and OSF and so on that are closed!

