In article <9304011608.AA25100@inet-gw-1.pa.dec.com>, MARK%6194.decnet@consrt.rockwell.com ("6194::MARK") writes:
> Does anyone know if it possible or not to configure PATHWORKS to allow
> submission of DCL .COM files from a PC to a VAX batch queue for processing 
> (say, SYS$BATCH) in a way similar to the way that you can configure PATHWORKS 
> to print jobs from a PC to VAX print queues?  If so, could you point me to
> the appropriate references in the documentation?  So far, I haven't seen
> anything like this mentioned.  Is this, perhaps, not allowed because of the
> security issues it raises?
> 
> We are using:
> 	VMS 5.5-2
> 	PATHWORKS 4.0
> 
> Mark Harcourt
> mark@gs1.cca.cr.rockwell.com
> Cedar Rapids, Iowa
> 
-- 
Mark,
 
Yes, even the older versions of Pathworks (the manual from 4.0 
happens to be handy at the moment) support this feature. 
 
The NFT utilities SUBMIT subcommand is the correct way to use 
this feature.
 
Occasionally, the default parameters used by SUBMIT/REMOTE may be 
inconvenient (like defaults on which print queue, whether to 
print the batch log on SYS$PRINT, and so on). If this is the 
case, it is not difficult to write a simple (in DCL) network 
server which will implement all of the features of SUBMIT/REMOTE, 
but still allowing choice (or at least indulgence of your 
personal preferences for defaults) for the various options 
available on the VMS SUBMIT command.
 
I hope that the above information is helpful. If I have been 
unclear, or if I can be of further assistance, please feel free 
to contact me via Email or phone.
 
