Nik Zapantis (zapantis@uvphys.phys.uvic.ca) wrote:


: I am testing DECFax mail for VMS, a product that allows you to send/receive
: faxes by using your VMS system and a fax modem.
: SPD indicates that DECFax only supports 3 fax modems, Murata, Dataplex
:and 
:HSL
: I would like to know if anyone has been able to use a US Robotics data/fax
: modem with this product ( I have not been able to get DECFax to talk to the
: my USR modem).

What I have found out about it is that DECfax Mail evidently uses 
"CCITT Group 3 / EIA TR.29 Class 2" fax capability. So, since there are
only a handful of modems out there that talk this language, then you 
are very limited; no normal (read: inexpensive) faxmodems will work. 

BTW, don't even think about buying a Dataplex faxmodem through DEC. They 
charge $950 for the Dataplex, and it lists for $600 from other sources. 
Of course, these other sources are in Australia. But given that AUS$600 
is ~US$400, and this is _list_ price, then I believe you can find it for 
about US$300 or so given the right contacts...

One possible alternative is the MultiTech line of faxmodems, which uses
that same TR.29 fax capability. If anyone ever tries one of these out, 
let me know what happens.


Chris
