In article <C4tGwH.G0D@news.cso.uiuc.edu>, jberg@pluto.ncsa.uiuc.edu writes...

>ULTRIX does not even adhere to the same floating point format standard as
>"all other U*ix's".  It's nice to be headache free at my (140+SPEC) HP735.
> 

Floating point support IS NOT a feature of an operating system, its a feature
of the hardware on which it runs. 

If you run ULTRIX on and older VAX, you will only get support for VAX floating
point, which is peculiar to VAX (and somwhat PDP-11) hardware whether you run
ULTRIX, VMS, VAXeln, or System V.

If you run ULTRIX on a DECsystem 5000, you will only get support for IEEE
floating point, which just about all new hardware (even DEC's new VAXen as well
as Alphas) supports.

